  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down Activity</title>
<para>The college student who is looking for a data plan for her cell phone found a third option, which also offers a 2-gigabyte monthly allowance for data.</para>
<para>The monthly cost of this option can be represented by function \(C\), defined by \(C(x)=30x+5\), where \(x\) is the gigabytes of data used over the monthly allowance.</para>
<!--Question 2 -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Find \(C(0.7)\) and explain what it means in this situation.</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  
  <para>Compare your answers:</para>
    
    <para>\(C(0.7)=26\) because \(30(0.7)+5=26\). Your answers
      may vary, but here is a possible explanation: It means that the cost would be $26 if she used 0.7 gigabyte over the 2-gigabytes allowance in a month.
   </para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Question 2 -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Her budget is still $50 a month. To find out how many gigabytes of data she could use if she chose this plan, she writes \(C(x)=50\) and solves for \(x\). What value of \(x\) makes this equation true? Be prepared to show your reasoning.</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  
  <para>Compare your answers:</para>
    
    <para>\(x=1.5\). Your answers may vary, but here is a possible explanation: Because \(C(x)=30x+5\), we can write \(C(x)=50\) as \(30x+5=50\) and solve for \(x\), which gives 1.5.</para>
  
  </solution></exercise></section>
